00:53:12,160 --> 00:53:13,410
so I want to show--

685
00:53:20,320 --> 00:53:21,940
yeah, sorry about that.

686
00:53:21,940 --> 00:53:23,460
This is not what
we want to prove.

687
00:53:23,460 --> 00:53:25,360
Sorry.

688
00:53:25,360 --> 00:53:27,880
Sorry, I should have said.

689
00:53:27,880 --> 00:53:28,720
Yeah.

690
00:53:28,720 --> 00:53:31,220
It's not these
functions that converge.

691
00:53:31,220 --> 00:53:33,560
It's the sum of them.

692
00:53:33,560 --> 00:53:36,000
So what I want to
prove is that--

693
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:38,560
I want to prove that
this thing here--

694
00:53:38,560 --> 00:53:45,780
as k equal to 0 to n,
that this function here

695
00:53:45,780 --> 00:53:50,270
converge uniformly.

696
00:53:50,270 --> 00:53:50,770
OK?

697
00:53:53,740 --> 00:53:56,140
So think about it.

698
00:53:56,140 --> 00:54:02,740
You want this to probably
apply to some power series.

699
00:54:02,740 --> 00:54:09,700
And so the individual fk
is like this polynomial.

700
00:54:09,700 --> 00:54:13,860
It's of some degree.

701
00:54:13,860 --> 00:54:16,100
OK.

702
00:54:16,100 --> 00:54:20,020
So we define this function Sn.

703
00:54:20,020 --> 00:54:26,170
And I want to prove this
Sn and then converge.

704
00:54:30,220 --> 00:54:33,660
And if it's OK, I
think it's better

705
00:54:33,660 --> 00:54:37,620
to call this something else
than little f, to call it S,

706
00:54:37,620 --> 00:54:40,800
because it's not these
guys that converge.

707
00:54:40,800 --> 00:54:42,270
It's the sum of
them that converge.

708
00:54:46,288 --> 00:54:52,910
So we want to show that these
guys here, the Sn converts

709
00:54:52,910 --> 00:54:54,640
to this S uniform.

710
00:54:59,310 --> 00:55:02,590
That's what we want to prove.

711
00:55:02,590 --> 00:55:06,830
Now, let's look
at the difference

712
00:55:06,830 --> 00:55:14,150
between Sn of x and Sm of x.

713
00:55:14,150 --> 00:55:21,710
And so here I'm going to think
about n as being larger than m.

714
00:55:21,710 --> 00:55:24,010
Suppose I'm thinking
about this thing here.

715
00:55:26,550 --> 00:55:32,910
Well, this here is when
you're summing the first--

716
00:55:32,910 --> 00:55:35,870
I guess you're starting
at k equal to 0.

717
00:55:35,870 --> 00:55:42,330
So then we're summing the
first n plus 1 of those guys.

718
00:55:42,330 --> 00:55:43,783
Here, we're summing more.

719
00:55:43,783 --> 00:55:45,450
We're summing those
guys, but then we're

720
00:55:45,450 --> 00:55:47,610
also summing some more.

721
00:55:47,610 --> 00:55:50,730
And so this thing here--

722
00:55:50,730 --> 00:55:52,710
so let me just write it out.

723
00:55:52,710 --> 00:55:59,450
So k equal to 0 to n of fk of x.

724
00:55:59,450 --> 00:56:03,250
And the second one is
