01:16:27,400 --> 01:16:29,260
from minus L to L.

1005
01:16:29,260 --> 01:16:32,460
Remember that L had
to be strictly less

1006
01:16:32,460 --> 01:16:36,836
than the radius of convergence.

1007
01:16:36,836 --> 01:16:39,660
And so this is extremely useful.

1008
01:16:39,660 --> 01:16:45,940
If you have-- and it will be
clear next time why it's useful

1009
01:16:45,940 --> 01:16:48,940
because if you have
uniform convergence,

1010
01:16:48,940 --> 01:16:51,580
then it becomes very easy--

1011
01:16:51,580 --> 01:16:53,660
if you have uniform
convergence, then you

1012
01:16:53,660 --> 01:16:56,620
can argue about if
you want to take

1013
01:16:56,620 --> 01:17:00,220
the derivative of integrating
this thing over here,

1014
01:17:00,220 --> 01:17:03,540
if you have uniform
convergence, then

1015
01:17:03,540 --> 01:17:08,100
it will say that then
a lot of operations

1016
01:17:08,100 --> 01:17:10,480
will be more precise
about that next time.

1017
01:17:10,480 --> 01:17:14,880
But a lot of operations, like
integration and differentiation,

1018
01:17:14,880 --> 01:17:19,580
you can do that over here
and then go to the limit.

1019
01:17:19,580 --> 01:17:24,520
So instead of if you were to
integrate this thing here.

1020
01:17:24,520 --> 01:17:29,120
So just say that-- but this
seems maybe very, very hard.

1021
01:17:29,120 --> 01:17:31,720
But the thing is, if
you can integrate here,

1022
01:17:31,720 --> 01:17:34,360
then you can just
use the usual sum,

1023
01:17:34,360 --> 01:17:36,720
